{
  "description": "Putting returned lines on an empty open bill (POS-12, PRD W6, D-006, POS spec §19): from one original bill (source kind `bill`, with each line's original as sold and what was returned of it before) or without a receipt (source kind `none`, with the price the approver set and what the counter suggested). Each returned line has a quantity, a reason (wrong_part, unused_option, defective, changed_mind, other) and a condition (resellable, defective). `needs` is what returnNeeds said; an approval (approver, reason, note, time) is required when it isn't empty, and covers every need, requested by the bill's seller. A linked line's refund is refundFor's; its unitPrice is that refund per whole unit (refund × 1 / qty, half away from zero). A no-receipt line's refund is qty × price. The result is the bill's `returns`. Errors, in order: bill_not_empty (lines or a return already there), empty_return, invalid_quantity, invalid_reason, note_required (other without a note), note_too_long (over 200), original_required (a linked line without its original), other_item, duplicate_line (one original line twice), return_over_quantity, price_required, return_approval_pending, and note_required for an approval with the reason other and no note. The seller is …f1.",
